1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,360
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time, known for bringing

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:09,040
his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:13,400
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon, once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:14,400
store.

5
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,280
Until one night, he decided to rewrite his story.

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:46,560
Today, I present you the Tarantino Method.

7
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:48,720
To follow this process, you'll need three things.

8
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,400
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night.

9
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:55,439
When the world is silent and not a soul is awake, that's when it can happen.

10
00:00:55,439 --> 00:00:56,439
Trust.

11
00:00:56,439 --> 00:00:57,439
Now it begins.

12
00:00:57,439 --> 00:01:00,680
The first page is always going to be the hardest, but it's really all about getting that ball

13
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:03,200
rolling.

14
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:08,680
Now that you've started, you have to ask yourself the big, scary, fear-mongering question.

15
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:10,639
What am I doing wrong?

16
00:01:10,639 --> 00:01:14,919
Be brutally honest, as Quentin himself would say, nail it.

17
00:01:14,919 --> 00:01:15,919
Take your time.

18
00:01:15,919 --> 00:01:16,919
Dive deep.

19
00:01:16,919 --> 00:01:17,919
It's gritty.

20
00:01:17,919 --> 00:01:18,919
It's tough.

21
00:01:18,919 --> 00:01:20,919
But it's absolutely necessary.

22
00:01:20,919 --> 00:01:27,080
And when you push through, boom, you're halfway there.

23
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,199
It's all out there.

24
00:01:28,199 --> 00:01:33,639
The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak, all laid out, bare for you

25
00:01:33,639 --> 00:01:34,760
to see.

26
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:39,559
Not built up in your mind, but on paper, tangible.

27
00:01:39,559 --> 00:01:44,680
Take a moment, because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it?

28
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:46,680
We're not all Quentin Tarantino.

29
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:49,000
You might be feeling like you're all written out.

30
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,519
So let's make this part simple, a straightforward list, a hundred ways you can change your life.

31
00:01:54,519 --> 00:01:56,360
Quite a simple process.

32
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:59,879
Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it.

33
00:01:59,879 --> 00:02:03,440
Repeat it over and over again and push forward.

34
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,440
Write it down.

35
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:10,199
Adapt, reflect, learn, and grow until finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my

36
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:11,199
life?

37
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:12,199
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

38
00:02:12,199 --> 00:02:15,759
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

39
00:02:15,759 --> 00:02:17,240
You gotta actually f***ing do it.


